122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Today, yoga is being taught in many different ways. While this has made yoga more accessible, it has also made it difficult for students to understand which qualifications are recognised, what standards are followed, and how to choose a credible teacher training program.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The Yoga Certification Board \(YCB\) was established by the Ministry of AYUSH, Government of India, to create a structured and nationally recognised framework for yoga education and certification. Its examinations assess not only your practical skills, but also your understanding of yoga philosophy, anatomy and physiology, teaching methodology, ethics, and the ability to guide others with confidence and responsibility.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Unlike courses that focus only on learning postures, the YCB pathway prepares you to become a knowledgeable and competent yoga teacher with a balanced understanding of both traditional wisdom and modern scientific principles.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (The YCB certification is recognised across India and is respected internationally. It opens opportunities to teach in yoga studios, wellness centres, schools, corporate organisations, retreats, and many other professional settings. More importantly, it gives you a strong educational foundation that supports lifelong learning in the field of yoga.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
